# ============================================================================
# JM MAKER SPORTSWEAR — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES TEMPLATE (.env.example)
# ============================================================================
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file to `.env.local` in the project root directory.
#   2. Replace the placeholder values below with your actual Supabase project
#      values from: Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Data API / API Keys.
#   3. Restart `npm run dev` so Vite loads your `.env.local` file.
#
# OFFLINE / LOCAL FALLBACK BEHAVIOR:
#   If `.env.local` is omitted or placeholders are left unchanged, the app
#   automatically runs in browser `localStorage` fallback mode (no cloud sync).
#
# SECURITY WARNING:
#   - NEVER commit `.env` or `.env.local` to Git (both are ignored in `.gitignore`).
#   - NEVER put a Supabase `service_role` or `sb_secret_...` key in ANY `VITE_*`
#     variable! All `VITE_*` variables are bundled into client-side JavaScript.
#   - Database access control is enforced server-side via PostgreSQL Row Level
#     Security (RLS) and `SECURITY DEFINER` RPCs.
# ============================================================================

# [REQUIRED for Supabase Cloud Mode | Frontend | Development & Production]
# Base URL of your Supabase project (do NOT append `/rest/v1/`).
# Source: Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Data API -> Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co

# [REQUIRED for Supabase Cloud Mode | Frontend | Development & Production]
# Public Publishable key (`sb_publishable_...`) or legacy `anon` public key.
# Safe for browser use ONLY because RLS is enabled on all 13 PostgreSQL tables.
# Source: Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-SUPABASE-PUBLISHABLE-OR-ANON-KEY
